{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-song-of-solomon-004",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 4,
  "title": "Song of Solomon 4",
  "display_title": "Song of Solomon 4",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "song-of-solomon",
  "book": "Song of Solomon",
  "bookName": "Song of Solomon",
  "bookOrder": 22,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 4,
  "sortOrder": 22004,
  "verseCount": 16,
  "aliases": [
    "Song",
    "Song of Songs",
    "SOS",
    "Canticles"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Behold, thou art fair, my love; behold, thou art fair; thou hast doves’ eyes within thy locks: thy hair is as a flock of goats, that appear from mount Gilead.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 4:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Thy teeth are like a flock of sheep that are even shorn, which came up from the washing; whereof every one bear twins, and none is barren among them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 4:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Thy lips are like a thread of scarlet, and thy speech is comely: thy temples are like a piece of a pomegranate within thy locks.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 4:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Thy neck is like the tower of David builded for an armoury, whereon there hang a thousand bucklers, all shields of mighty men.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 4:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Thy two breasts are like two young roes that are twins, which feed among the lilies.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 4:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Until the day break, and the shadows flee away, I will get me to the mountain of myrrh, and to the hill of frankincense.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 4:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Thou art all fair, my love; there is no spot in thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 4:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Come with me from Lebanon, my spouse, with me from Lebanon: look from the top of Amana, from the top of Shenir and Hermon, from the lions’ dens, from the mountains of the leopards.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 4:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Thou hast ravished my heart, my sister, my spouse; thou hast ravished my heart with one of thine eyes, with one chain of thy neck.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 4:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "How fair is thy love, my sister, my spouse! how much better is thy love than wine! and the smell of thine ointments than all spices!",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 4:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Thy lips, O my spouse, drop as the honeycomb: honey and milk are under thy tongue; and the smell of thy garments is like the smell of Lebanon.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 4:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "A garden inclosed is my sister, my spouse; a spring shut up, a fountain sealed.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 4:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Thy plants are an orchard of pomegranates, with pleasant fruits; camphire, with spikenard,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 4:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Spikenard and saffron; calamus and cinnamon, with all trees of frankincense; myrrh and aloes, with all the chief spices:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 4:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "A fountain of gardens, a well of living waters, and streams from Lebanon.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 4:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Awake, O north wind; and come, thou south; blow upon my garden, that the spices thereof may flow out. Let my beloved come into his garden, and eat his pleasant fruits.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 4:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:4:16"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
